[Title "English Opening"]
[Description "A hypermodern opening controlling d5 from the flank without committing central pawns."]
[PlayerColor "WHITE"]
[VariationTitle "Four Knights, Bremen System"]
[VariationDescription "King's English 1...e5 line developing four knights with White fianchettoing on g3."]

1. c4 {Controls the key central d5 square from the flank without committing central pawns.} e5 2. Nc3 {Develops the knight to reinforce control over d5 and e4.} Nf6 3. g3 {Prepares to fianchetto the light-squared bishop on g2 along the long diagonal.} Nc6 4. Bg2 {Places the bishop on the long diagonal (h1-a8), exerting indirect pressure on d5 and Black's queenside.} Bc5 5. Nf3 {Develops the knight towards the center, preparing kingside castling and controlling e5/d4.} d6 6. O-O {Tucks the king safely into the corner and activates the f1 rook for central action.} O-O 7. d3 {Solidifies c4 and e4 while opening the c1-h6 diagonal for the dark-squared bishop.} a6 8. a3 h6 9. b4 Ba7 10. Bb2 Be6 *

